      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "What is $\\sqrt[3]{9}$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The radical $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ can be written using a fractional exponent as ${x}^{1/n}.$\n\nComparing $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ with $\\sqrt[3]{9},$ we get $x=9,$ and $n=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{9}={9}^{1/3}\n$$",
